# ============================================
# Issue: NATS authentication error
# Captured: 2026-06-07
# Source: kubectl logs nats-0 -c nats --tail=100 | grep -i auth
# Severity: error
# ============================================
# Symptom: Even after fixing CoreDNS, the kube-watch connection fails
# with auth errors because it sends the hardcoded credentials
# zeabur-kube-watch:<REDACTED> but the NATS ConfigMap requires nothing
# OR a different credential.

[1] 2026/06/07 14:35:01.123 [ERR] 127.0.0.1:54321 - client connection closed: Authorization Violation
[2] 2026/06/07 14:35:01.234 [ERR] 127.0.0.1:54322 - client connection closed: Authorization Violation
[3] 2026/06/07 14:35:01.345 [ERR] 127.0.0.1:54323 - client connection closed: Authorization Violation
[4] 2026/06/07 14:35:01.456 [INF] Listening for client connections on 0.0.0.0:4222
[5] 2026/06/07 14:35:01.567 [ERR] 127.0.0.1:54324 - client connection closed: User zeabur-kube-watch not found

# ============================================
# Analysis
# ============================================
# - Zeabur's NATS ConfigMap has auth enabled with user: admin
# - kube-watch sends user: zeabur-kube-watch (hardcoded)
# - Even if we add user `zeabur-kube-watch` to NATS config, we don't know the password
# - The password <REDACTED> is in the binary, but we can't read it
#
# Decision: Disable NATS auth entirely. This is a dev environment, single-tenant.
# Production would need proper NATS auth, which would require modifying
# the kube-watch binary or asking Zeabur to add env var support.
